Subject: [PATCH 02579/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A1
 (HEADLINE; oracle-distinct LOCALIZER; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- VERIFIABLE
 PROCESS DATA SYNTHESIS + contrastive earliest-error LOCALIZER
 (arXiv:2605.02395 VERIFIED 'Controllable and Verifiable Process Data
 Synthesis for Process Reward Models', the .405 SOTA-ingestion
 flagged_for_v406). .405 (exp4381) PROVED the detector DETECTS trace-level
 errors (AUROC 0.92-0.98) but CANNOT LOCALIZE the earliest causal error
 (first-error F1 0.096, IDENTICAL across unidirectional/bidirectional/causal
 -> bidirectional fusion is a measured no-op, delta CI95 [0,0], 103/114
 missed). The paper's OWN finding: 'first-error localization remains
 substantially more challenging than overall step classification' -- the .405
 null is a DATA problem (no ground-truth first-error supervision), NOT a
 fusion-method problem. THE FIX: SYNTHESIZE verifiable process data -- (1)
 take/construct a correct symbolic reasoning chain, (2) inject a
 template-aware error at a KNOWN intermediate step, (3) recompute subsequent
 steps under the corrupted state, (4) VERIFY the injected step is NOT
 derivable from its prefix (prefix-invalid, trajectory-consistent) ->
 ground-truth earliest-error labels. Train a CONTRASTIVE earliest-error
 localizer on those labels. EVALUATE first-error localization F1 on a HELD-OUT
 REAL FoVer split AND the GAP-4 ARC split vs the .405 ensemble baseline
 (0.096). (5) ABSTENTION: report a STRUCTURED report/abstain signal
 (Prover-Verifier-Deliberation 2605.25133 -- accept only localizer verdicts
 that survive a bounded checkable-subclaim challenge) alongside the
 raw-threshold risk-coverage curve. Emit localizer_beats_ensemble_baseline
 BARE bool := (the synthetic-data-trained localizer's first-error F1 on the
 HELD-OUT REAL split exceeds the .405 ensemble baseline 0.096, delta
 CI95-excl-0, on >=1 domain). verifier_is_oracle=false (a learned localizer
 scored against ground-truth-labeled candidates; the symbolic/executable check
 defines correctness, the localizer estimates WHICH step -- oracle-distinct).
 A win = the detector graduates 'detects'->'localizes the earliest error',
 cross-domain; a clean null (synthetic data does not transfer to the real
 first-error distribution) is decision-grade + logs the residual as a
 missing-verifier gap. Cached + CPU; symbolic synthesis needs no live LLM. NO
 TRM training.

